IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nt-pit`
IMPORT `nt-pit-duties`

-- Northwest Territories Income Tax Act -- the resident individual's questions, and the parent's questions about the NWT
-- Child Benefit and the Cost of Living Offset. Every question calls the rules in nt-pit.l4 and nt-pit-duties.l4; nothing
-- is restated here. Plain inputs, one per fact the person can state. Federal amounts (taxable income, net income, the
-- federal credit bases, adjusted income) come from the person's federal return or notice of assessment; see the federal
-- Income Tax Act encoding in subjects/ca/income-tax-act/. The indexed credit amounts are the territory's figures for the
-- year, as printed on the NWT personal tax credits return (TD1NT) or the NWT tax form (NOTES.md finding 2).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Do I pay Northwest Territories income tax`

@export Am I liable to Northwest Territories income tax for the year under s 2(1) of the Income Tax Act?
GIVEN `I lived in the Northwest Territories on December 31` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were resident in the Northwest Territories on the last day of the taxation year (31 December)
      `I earned income in the Northwest Territories` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, while not resident there on 31 December, you had income earned in the year in the Northwest Territories (for example from employment or a business there)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I liable to NWT income tax` IF
    `is liable to Northwest Territories income tax under s 2(1)` `I lived in the Northwest Territories on December 31` `I earned income in the Northwest Territories`

§ `My territorial tax`

@export What is my Northwest Territories tax for 2026, before credits, under s 2.11 of the Income Tax Act?
GIVEN `I lived in the Northwest Territories on December 31` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were resident in the Northwest Territories on 31 December 2026
      `I had income earned outside the Northwest Territories` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any of your 2026 income was earned outside the Northwest Territories (in a province, another territory or outside Canada), which brings in the apportionment of s 2.44
      `my taxable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your 2026 taxable income as computed for federal income tax (line 26000 of your return), in Canadian dollars
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`What is my NWT tax before credits for 2026` MEANS
    CONSIDER `why the tax is not covered` `I lived in the Northwest Territories on December 31` `I had income earned outside the Northwest Territories` 2026 `my taxable income`
    WHEN JUST r THEN `not covered` r
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `answered` (`the tax under s 2.11(4)` `my taxable income` `the 2026 thresholds published by the Canada Revenue Agency`)

@export What is my Northwest Territories tax before credits for another year, given that year's tier thresholds, under s 2.11 of the Income Tax Act?
GIVEN `the tax year` IS A NUMBER @desc The taxation year, 2005 or later
      `I lived in the Northwest Territories on December 31` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were resident in the Northwest Territories on 31 December of that year
      `I had income earned outside the Northwest Territories` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any of your income for the year was earned outside the Northwest Territories
      `my taxable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your taxable income for the year as computed for federal income tax, in Canadian dollars
      `the year's tier one threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The NWT tier one threshold for the year (the top of the 5.9% bracket), as published for that year
      `the year's tier two threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The NWT tier two threshold for the year (the top of the 8.6% bracket)
      `the year's tier three threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The NWT tier three threshold for the year (the top of the 12.2% bracket)
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`What is my NWT tax before credits for a given year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `why the tax is not covered` `I lived in the Northwest Territories on December 31` `I had income earned outside the Northwest Territories` `the tax year` `my taxable income`
    WHEN JUST r THEN `not covered` r
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `answered` (`the tax under s 2.11(4)` `my taxable income` (`Thresholds` WITH `tier one threshold` IS `the year's tier one threshold`, `tier two threshold` IS `the year's tier two threshold`, `tier three threshold` IS `the year's tier three threshold`))

§ `My territorial credits`

DECLARE `My household` IS ONE OF
    `I am single with no eligible dependant`
    `I support my spouse or common-law partner`
    `I am single and support an eligible dependant`

@export What is my Northwest Territories basic credit (single status, spouse or eligible dependant) under ss 2.14 to 2.16 of the Income Tax Act?
GIVEN `my household` IS A `My household` @desc Your situation during the year: "I am single with no eligible dependant"; "I support my spouse or common-law partner" (married or common-law, supporting them, and not separated because of a breakdown); or "I am single and support an eligible dependant" (unmarried, keeping a home where you live with and wholly support a related person under 18, or infirm, or your parent or grandparent)
      `the other person's net income` IS A NUMBER @desc The net income for the year of your spouse or common-law partner, or of the eligible dependant, in Canadian dollars; 0 if you are single with no eligible dependant
      `the NWT basic personal amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The Northwest Territories basic personal amount for the year (the indexed $11,050 of the Act), as printed on the NWT forms for the year, in Canadian dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my NWT basic credit` MEANS
    `the basic credits under ss 2.14 to 2.16` `the NWT basic personal amount` h
    WHERE
        h MEANS CONSIDER `my household`
                WHEN `I am single with no eligible dependant` THEN `single, with no eligible dependant`
                WHEN `I support my spouse or common-law partner` THEN `supporting a spouse or common-law partner` `the other person's net income`
                WHEN `I am single and support an eligible dependant` THEN `single, supporting an eligible dependant under s 2.15` `the other person's net income`

@export What is my Northwest Territories age credit under s 2.2 of the Income Tax Act?
GIVEN `I was 65 or over by the end of the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you reached 65 before the end of the taxation year
      `my net income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your net income for the year (line 23600), in Canadian dollars
      `the NWT age amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The Northwest Territories age amount for the year (the indexed $5,405), as printed on the NWT forms, in Canadian dollars
      `the NWT age amount income threshold` IS A NUMBER @desc The income above which the NWT age amount is reduced by 15% (the indexed $26,941), in Canadian dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my NWT age credit` MEANS
    `the age credit under s 2.2` `I was 65 or over by the end of the year` `my net income` `the NWT age amount` `the NWT age amount income threshold`

@export What is my Northwest Territories pension credit under s 2.21 of the Income Tax Act?
GIVEN `I lived in the Northwest Territories on December 31` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were resident in the Northwest Territories on 31 December
      `my eligible pension income` IS A NUMBER @desc The pension income amount you used for the federal pension income credit (federal s 118(3)), in Canadian dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my NWT pension credit` MEANS
    `the pension credit under s 2.21` `I lived in the Northwest Territories on December 31` `my eligible pension income`

@export What is my Northwest Territories charitable donations credit under s 2.22 of the Income Tax Act?
GIVEN `my gifts claimed federally` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of your gifts used for the federal charitable donations credit (federal s 118.1) for the year, in Canadian dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my NWT donations credit` MEANS `the donations credit under s 2.22` `my gifts claimed federally`

@export What is my Northwest Territories disability credit under s 2.24(1) of the Income Tax Act (for a person 18 or over)?
GIVEN `I can claim the federal disability tax credit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are entitled to the federal disability tax credit for yourself under federal s 118.3(1) (you hold an approved disability tax credit certificate)
      `the NWT disability amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The Northwest Territories disability amount for the year (the indexed $8,961), as printed on the NWT forms, in Canadian dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my NWT disability credit` MEANS
    `the disability credit under s 2.24(1) for an adult` `I can claim the federal disability tax credit` `the NWT disability amount`

@export What is my Northwest Territories education credit under s 2.26 of the Income Tax Act?
GIVEN `months I was enrolled full-time` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of months in the year you were enrolled full-time in a qualifying educational program at a designated educational institution
      `other months I was enrolled part-time` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of other months you were enrolled in a specified (part-time) program requiring at least 12 hours of courses in the month, with the enrolment certificate filed
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my NWT education credit` MEANS
    `the education credit under s 2.26` `months I was enrolled full-time` `other months I was enrolled part-time`

@export What are my Northwest Territories credits for tuition, student loan interest, and CPP contributions and EI premiums under ss 2.25, 2.28 and 2.29 of the Income Tax Act?
GIVEN `my eligible tuition` IS A NUMBER @desc The tuition amount you use for the year under federal s 118.5, in Canadian dollars; 0 if none
      `my student loan interest` IS A NUMBER @desc The student loan interest you claim for the year under federal s 118.62, in Canadian dollars; 0 if none
      `my CPP contributions and EI premiums` IS A NUMBER @desc The Canada Pension Plan base contributions and employment insurance premiums that give you the federal s 118.7 credit, in Canadian dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What are my NWT tuition, interest and contribution credits` MEANS
    `a credit at the appropriate percentage` (`my eligible tuition` PLUS `my student loan interest` PLUS `my CPP contributions and EI premiums`)

@export What is my Northwest Territories dividend tax credit under s 2.32 of the Income Tax Act?
GIVEN `I lived in the Northwest Territories on December 31` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were resident in the Northwest Territories on 31 December
      `my taxable amount of other than eligible dividends` IS A NUMBER @desc The taxable (grossed-up) amount of dividends other than eligible dividends included in your income, in Canadian dollars
      `my taxable amount of eligible dividends` IS A NUMBER @desc The taxable (grossed-up) amount of eligible dividends included in your income, in Canadian dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my NWT dividend credit` MEANS
    `the dividend deduction under s 2.32` `I lived in the Northwest Territories on December 31` `my taxable amount of other than eligible dividends` `my taxable amount of eligible dividends`

@export What is my Northwest Territories tax payable after credits?
GIVEN `my NWT tax before credits` IS A NUMBER @desc Your NWT tax before credits (see the tax question), in Canadian dollars
      `my basic credit` IS A NUMBER @desc Your NWT basic credit (single status, spouse or eligible dependant)
      `my age credit` IS A NUMBER @desc Your NWT age credit; 0 if none
      `my pension credit` IS A NUMBER @desc Your NWT pension credit; 0 if none
      `my donations credit` IS A NUMBER @desc Your NWT charitable donations credit; 0 if none
      `my disability credit` IS A NUMBER @desc Your NWT disability credit; 0 if none
      `my education, tuition, interest and contribution credits` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of your NWT education, tuition, student loan interest and CPP/EI credits; 0 if none
      `my dividend credit` IS A NUMBER @desc Your NWT dividend tax credit; 0 if none
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my NWT tax payable` MEANS
    `the tax payable after credits` `my NWT tax before credits`
        (`my basic credit` PLUS `my age credit` PLUS `my pension credit` PLUS `my donations credit` PLUS `my disability credit` PLUS `my education, tuition, interest and contribution credits` PLUS `my dividend credit`)

§ `Filing and paying`

@export Must I file a Northwest Territories income tax return for the year (s 11 of the Income Tax Act, applying federal s 150)?
GIVEN `I owe NWT tax for the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any tax is payable by you under the NWT Income Tax Act for the year
      `I had a taxable capital gain or sold capital property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had a taxable capital gain or disposed of capital property in the year
      `I have a Home Buyers' Plan or Lifelong Learning Plan balance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had a positive HBP or LLP balance at the end of the year
      `the CRA asked me to file` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister of National Revenue demanded a return from you by written notice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I file an NWT return` IF
    `I must file a return under s 11 and federal s 150` `I owe NWT tax for the year` `I had a taxable capital gain or sold capital property` `I have a Home Buyers' Plan or Lifelong Learning Plan balance` `the CRA asked me to file`

@export By what date must I file my return for the year (s 11 of the Income Tax Act, applying federal s 150(1)(d))?
GIVEN `the tax year` IS A NUMBER @desc The taxation year, for example 2026
      `I or my spouse ran a business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, or your cohabiting spouse or common-law partner, carried on a business in the year (not primarily tax shelter investments)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I file` MEANS `the filing due date` `the tax year` `I or my spouse ran a business`

@export By what date must I pay the rest of my tax for the year (ss 16(1)(b) and 17 of the Income Tax Act; the federal balance-due day)?
GIVEN `the tax year` IS A NUMBER @desc The taxation year, for example 2026
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I pay the balance` MEANS `the balance-due day` `the tax year`

@export If I must pay by instalments, how much is each quarterly instalment under s 16(1)(a) of the Income Tax Act?
GIVEN `the tax I estimate or last year's tax` IS A NUMBER @desc Either your estimate of this year's NWT tax payable or your NWT tax payable for last year, whichever you choose as the base, in Canadian dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is each instalment` MEANS `each quarterly instalment under s 16(1)(a)` `the tax I estimate or last year's tax`

§ `NWT Child Benefit`

@export Am I an eligible individual for the NWT Child Benefit in respect of a child, under s 3.1 of the Income Tax Act?
GIVEN `I live with the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you reside with the child
      `I am resident in the Northwest Territories` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are resident in the Northwest Territories
      `my care of the child` IS A `Care of the child` @desc Whether you are the parent who primarily fulfils the responsibility for the child's care and upbringing, a shared custody parent (living with the child on an equal or near-equal basis with the other parent, who is not your cohabiting spouse), or neither
      `I am a foreign official or their family` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are exempt from Canadian tax as an officer or servant of another country, or a member of their family, under federal s 149(1)(a) or (b)
      `I or my spouse meet the status requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or your cohabiting spouse or common-law partner is a Canadian citizen, a permanent resident, a protected person, in a humanitarian designated class, or a temporary resident who has lived in Canada for the previous 18 months
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an eligible individual for the NWT Child Benefit` IF
    `is an eligible individual under s 3.1` `I live with the child` `I am resident in the Northwest Territories` `my care of the child` `I am a foreign official or their family` `I or my spouse meet the status requirement`

@export Is this child a qualified dependant for the NWT Child Benefit under s 3.1 of the Income Tax Act?
GIVEN `the child's age` IS A NUMBER @desc The child's age in whole years
      `the child lives with me in the Northwest Territories` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child resides with you (the eligible individual) in the Northwest Territories
      `the child's own spouse claimed the spouse amount for them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child's own cohabiting spouse or common-law partner claimed the federal spouse amount for the child
      `a children's special allowance is paid for the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a special allowance under the Children's Special Allowances Act (for a child in care) is payable for the child
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the child a qualified dependant` IF
    `is a qualified dependant under s 3.1` `the child's age` `the child lives with me in the Northwest Territories` `the child's own spouse claimed the spouse amount for them` `a children's special allowance is paid for the child`

@export How much NWT Child Benefit do I get for a month, under ss 3.2 and 3.2(2.1) of the Income Tax Act and s 1.1 of the Income Tax Regulations?
GIVEN `I am an eligible individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an eligible individual for the child or children at the beginning of the month (see the eligibility question)
      `I filed my return for the base year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you filed your income tax return for the base taxation year (the year before last for January to June payments, last year for July to December)
      `my spouse filed if asked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your cohabiting spouse or common-law partner filed a return for that year, if the CRA demanded one (true if not demanded)
      `I lived in the NWT at the start of the month and the day before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were resident in the Northwest Territories at the beginning of the month and on the last day of the month before
      `I applied in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you filed the benefit application (the prescribed notice) within 11 months after the end of the month, or the CRA extended the time
      `my family's adjusted income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your adjusted family net income for the base taxation year (your net income plus that of your cohabiting spouse or common-law partner, as for the federal Canada child benefit), in Canadian dollars
      `children under six` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of your qualified dependants had not reached six at the beginning of the month
      `children six or over` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of your qualified dependants were six or over (and under 18) at the beginning of the month
      `my care of the children` IS A `Care of the child` @desc Whether you are the parent who primarily fulfils the responsibility for the children's care and upbringing, or a shared custody parent
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much NWT Child Benefit do I get this month` MEANS
    IF     `I am an eligible individual`
       AND `the conditions of s 3.2(1) and s 3.3(1) are met` `I filed my return for the base year` `my spouse filed if asked` `I lived in the NWT at the start of the month and the day before` `I applied in time`
    THEN `the monthly NWT Child Benefit for my care arrangement` (`the monthly overpayment under s 3.2(2)` `my family's adjusted income` `children under six` `children six or over`) `my care of the children`
    ELSE 0

@export Which taxation year's income is used for my NWT Child Benefit for a month (the base taxation year, s 3.1)?
GIVEN `the month` IS A NUMBER @desc The month of the payment, 1 (January) to 12 (December)
      `the calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year of the payment, for example 2026
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Which year's income counts for my NWT Child Benefit` MEANS `the base taxation year` `the month` `the calendar year`

@export By what date must I have applied for the NWT Child Benefit for a given month (s 3.3(1) of the Income Tax Act)?
GIVEN `the month` IS A NUMBER @desc The month for which you want the benefit, 1 (January) to 12 (December)
      `the year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year of that month
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I apply for a month of NWT Child Benefit` MEANS `the last day to file the s 3.3(1) notice for a month` `the month` `the year`

@export If I stop being an eligible individual for a child, by what date must I tell the CRA (s 3.3(3) of the Income Tax Act)?
GIVEN `the day I stopped being eligible` IS A DATE @desc The date on which you ceased to be an eligible individual for the child (for example the child moved out); not needed if the child turned 18
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I report that I stopped being eligible` MEANS `the last day to notify under s 3.3(3)` `the day I stopped being eligible`

§ `Cost of Living Offset`

@export How much Cost of Living Offset is paid to me for a specified month under s 3.5 of the Income Tax Act and s 1.2 of the Income Tax Regulations?
GIVEN `I am 18 or over, or have been a parent living with my child or married or common-law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were 18 before the month, or at some earlier time were a parent living with your child or married or in a common-law partnership
      `I lived in the NWT on the first day of this and the previous specified month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were resident in the Northwest Territories on the first day of the specified month and of the preceding specified month
      `I filed my return for the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you filed your income tax return for the taxation year
      `my zone` IS AN `Offset zone` @desc The zone of your ordinary residence under s 1.2 of the regulations: Zone 1 (for example Yellowknife, Hay River, Fort Smith), Zone 2 (for example Inuvik, Behchoko, Fort Simpson) or Zone 3 (Norman Wells, Paulatuk, Sachs Harbour, Tulita, Ulukhaktok)
      `I have a spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a qualified relation (cohabiting spouse or common-law partner) for the month
      `my qualified dependants` IS A NUMBER @desc How many qualified dependants (children under 18 living with you) you have for the month
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much Cost of Living Offset do I get` MEANS
    IF `is entitled to the offset under s 3.5(3)` `I am 18 or over, or have been a parent living with my child or married or common-law` `I lived in the NWT on the first day of this and the previous specified month` `I filed my return for the year`
    THEN `the offset deemed paid in a specified month` `my zone` `I have a spouse or common-law partner` `my qualified dependants`
    ELSE 0
